From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:18:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: refuse page-less dma-buf exports for static importers
 too

nv_dma_buf_attach() only rejected an importer without peer2peer support
when it had importer_ops. dma_buf_attach() leaves importer_ops NULL and
peer2peer false, so a static importer, which never declared it can handle
peer resources, got an sg table with no struct pages. An importer calling
sg_page() on it would oops.

Check peer2peer alone, as the dma-buf rules require. Exports with struct
pages are not affected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c
index c2967668..6249f1e9 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dmabuf.c
@@ -1030,8 +1030,7 @@ nv_dma_buf_attach(
     }
 
 #if defined(NV_DMA_BUF_ATTACHMENT_HAS_PEER2PEER)
-    if ((attachment->importer_ops != NULL) &&
-        (!attachment->peer2peer) &&
+    if ((!attachment->peer2peer) &&
         (!priv->map_attrs.mem_has_struct_page))
     {
         nv_printf(NV_DBG_ERRORS,
